# The allowlist of tests/retired_words.rs (RFC 003 D-6; INC-3): a message may not use a word that
# `docs/glossary.md` section 3.1 retires, except where the word is not ours to change. Reviewed like code: a
# line added here is a decision.
#
# key :: term :: reason
#   key     the message key (for example `verify.intro`)
#   term    the retired word the message is allowed to contain, as the glossary lists it
#   reason  why it is legitimate (the name of a command in operator text, data owned by prikk, …)
#
# A message whose key starts `explain.` is an explanation the reader opens on demand and needs no line here.
# An entry that no message needs any more fails the test, so this file cannot collect dead lines. It is empty
# today: no message of either catalog uses a retired word, except the one label below.

# The word Verified is prikk's, for the history alone (RFC 005 part 2 D-7): the label of the verification badge, which
# the badge and the verification page print, and no other message.
assurance.verified :: verified :: the label of the verification badge: prikk's word for the history alone, never said of a claim, a source or a view
assurance.verified :: 検証済み :: the Japanese label of the verification badge: prikk's word for the history alone, never said of a claim, a source or a view
